// features: arrays, known-divergence, locals, print, string-literal, structs, vec-push
// Struct copies under move-append takes (VM-correct values).
//
// KNOWN DIVERGENCE (native): `t := s` shares struct identity on native
// (`zz_clone` bumps only the object header, never field buffers, while
// `zz_release_object` frees them), so mutating the copy's field is also
// visible through the source. The VM deep-copies (value semantics) and
// prints s_len=1 then t_len=2. Tracked in `known_native_failure` as
// "move_append_struct_copy"; fix options are documented in
// docs/perf/append-elision-report.md (deep-bump retain vs COW field
// write). The `zz_object_push_field_take` in-place path gates on the
// field buffer counter so takes never corrupt a getter-extracted live
// share (the `a` case below prints a_len=1 on both).
//
// NOTE: values print as `name=value` (not bare numbers) so the
// dual-engine parity harness — which strips purely-numeric lines —
// actually compares them.
struct W2 { f: [int] }
s := W2{f: [1]}
t := s
t.f = vec.push(t.f, 2)
println("s_len={len(s.f)}")
println("t_len={len(t.f)}")

// Getter-extracted share stays intact on both engines.
u := W2{f: [1]}
a := u.f
u.f = vec.push(u.f, 9)
println("a_len={len(a)}")
println("u_len={len(u.f)}")

println("move_append_struct_copy_ok")
